BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:0f867f0c-5422-4d44-93b8-d7faaae7019b@spacex-launch-alerts
DTSTAMP:20261109T230616Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261109T230616Z
SEQUENCE:216428776
SUMMARY:🚀 [TBC] Starship · Starlink Group 31-2 (Starship Flight 15)
DTSTART:20261113T224500Z
DTEND:20261114T000000Z
LOCATION:Orbital Launch Pad 2\, SpaceX Starbase\, TX\, USA
DESCRIPTION:Status: To Be Confirmed\nWindow: Fri\, 13 Nov 2026 22:45:00 UTC
  – Sat\, 14 Nov 2026 00:00:00 UTC\nOrbit: Low Earth Orbit\nPad: Orbital 
 Launch Pad 2\, SpaceX Starbase\, TX\, USA\n\n15th test flight of the two-s
 tage Starship launch vehicle and 4th flight of Starship V3. Second Starshi
 p flight to deploy satellites (a group of Starlink satellites known as Sta
 rlink Group 31-2) into stable Low Earth Orbit and first ever to attempt re
 turning the Starship 2nd stage back to the launch site.\n\nThe ship is exp
 ected to fly at an altitude approximately 275 km above Earth and complete 
 approximately 14 orbits around the planet for more than 22 hours\, with th
 e ship expected to attempt returning back to Starbase\, Texas on its launc
 h pad by pad arms catching.\n\nThe booster’s primary test objective on F
 light 15 will be executing a successful launch\, ascent\, stage separation
 \, boostback burn\, and landing by pad arms catching. This will also be th
 e 1st Starship V3 booster to attempt returning to its launch site.\n\nStar
 ship will deliver 26 Starlink V3 satellites to orbit for the second time\,
  which aim to greatly expand the network's capacity and user speeds. Each 
 Starlink V3 satellite will add 1 Tbps of capacity to the constellation. 3 
 of the satellites have been modified with a suite of cameras to scan Stars
 hip’s heatshield and transmit imagery down to operators.\n\nCountdown & 
 updates: https://benjaminowens612.github.io/spacex-launch-alerts/#0f867f0c
 -5422-4d44-93b8-d7faaae7019b
URL:https://benjaminowens612.github.io/spacex-launch-alerts/#0f867f0c-5422-
 4d44-93b8-d7faaae7019b
CATEGORIES:starlink,starship
STATUS:TENTATIVE
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
